# Rust build artifacts
/target/
/target-*/

# Stores a test or a local run left behind. dc-store's suites write to the
# system temp directory, not here, but `dcstore --db` will happily point at a
# path inside the workspace and a committed lease database would hand every
# checkout someone else's active leases.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db

# Mutation testing run output (regenerate with cargo mutants)
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Generated coverage dump. Not source; paths go stale the moment the tree moves.
lcov.info

# testdata is extractor *input*, not build output.
#
# This workspace sits inside a repository whose root ignore patterns (`lib/`,
# `build/`, `var/`, `dist/`, `share/`) would otherwise govern fixture files:
# `testdata/vendor/lib/x.py` silently stopped being walked and the testdata
# determinism digest moved. Language fixtures legitimately use those directory
# names, so re-include the whole tree here — a nested ignore file takes
# precedence over the parent's, and the directory must be re-included before
# any file inside it can be.
!testdata/
!testdata/**
# …but never the generated stores or OS cruft that live inside fixtures.
testdata/**/.devcouncil/
testdata/**/.DS_Store
